  "title": "Saudi Arabia's Pipeline and Houthi Attacks in Yemen",
  "summary": "Saudi Arabia's decision to shut down its key oil pipeline has raised concerns about potential global supply disruptions, while Iran-backed militant groups have intensified their attacks in recent days. Saudi-led coalition launched strikes on Houthi-controlled Hodeidah governorate, while Iran-backed Houthi rebels claimed a missile attack on Saudi Arabian cities, wounding over 70 people and setting oil facilities ablaze, with Saudi Arabia promising retaliation. The attacks also led to a deadly Houthi missile attack on the Riyadh airport, killing 13 people and injuring over 300.",
